================================================================================
SCOPE NOTE — THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
================================================================================

The CC BY 4.0 licence above applies to the *curated and derived* content in
this repository — including but not limited to:

  * Ontology-based classifications and method tags
    (`classified_scopus.csv`, `final_ai4chips_high_only.csv` + `.json`,
     `pivot_*.csv`)
  * Hand-curated gists, stage summaries, acronym glossary, shortlist tables
    (`gists.json`, `stage_summaries.json`, `acronyms.md`,
     `stage_shortlists*.md`)
  * Geographic forecasts and narrative drafts
    (`geo_forecast.*`, `geo_leadership.md`, `geo_paper_section.md`,
     `conclusion_digital_thread.md`)
  * Manuscript reference artefacts
    (`references.bib`, `references_ieee.*`, `references_lookup.md`,
     `existing_refs.json`)
  * All figures in `figures/`

The following content is NOT licensed by this file and remains subject to
the terms of its original rights-holder:

  * Raw Scopus bibliographic records
    (`raw_scopus_*.jsonl`, `raw_scopus_*.csv`, `abstracts_cache.json`
     entries sourced from Scopus, and any fields propagated downstream
     from those records).
    These are governed by Elsevier's Scopus API terms of use:
        https://dev.elsevier.com/policy.html
    Redistribution may be restricted; users intending to redistribute
    or build on these fields should consult Elsevier's policy directly.

  * OpenAlex-sourced metadata
    (`openalex_cache/`, `external_references_cache/`, `abstracts_cache.json`
     entries sourced from OpenAlex).
    These are made available by OpenAlex under CC0:
        https://docs.openalex.org/additional-help/faq#how-is-openalex-licensed

By reusing this dataset, you accept responsibility for complying with the
licence terms of the underlying third-party content where applicable.

